---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { site, hasAddress, fullAddress } from '../config/site';

const officer = site.grievanceOfficer;

const toc = [
  { id: 'who-we-are', label: 'Who we are' },
  { id: 'information-we-collect', label: 'Information we collect' },
  { id: 'how-we-use-it', label: 'How we use it' },
  { id: 'product-data', label: 'Data in our products' },
  { id: 'sharing', label: 'Sharing and disclosure' },
  { id: 'retention', label: 'Data retention' },
  { id: 'security', label: 'Security' },
  { id: 'your-rights', label: 'Your rights' },
  { id: 'cookies', label: 'Cookies' },
  { id: 'children', label: 'Children' },
  { id: 'grievance-officer', label: 'Grievance Officer' },
  { id: 'changes', label: 'Changes' },
];
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Rachna Softech LLP collects, uses and protects personal data across its website and products, in line with India's Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023."
  summary="We collect only what we need to run our website and products, the data you put into our products stays yours, and we never sell personal data."
  toc={toc}
>
  <p>
    This Privacy Policy explains how {site.legalName} (“<strong>Rachna Labs</strong>”, “<strong>we</strong>”, “<strong>us</strong>”) collects,
    uses, shares and protects personal data when you visit this website, contact us or use our products. It is published in accordance with the
    Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 (“<strong>DPDP Act</strong>”), the Information Technology Act, 2000 and the rules made under them.
  </p>

  <h2 id="who-we-are">1. Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    {site.legalName} is a limited liability partnership registered in India{site.llpin && ` (LLPIN: ${site.llpin})`}{
      hasAddress && `, with its registered office at ${fullAddress}`
    }. We build and operate apps and software products. For personal data collected through this website and our apps, we are the Data Fiduciary
    under the DPDP Act.
  </p>

  <h2 id="information-we-collect">2. Information we collect</h2>
  <h3>Information you give us</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Contact and enquiry details:</strong> your name, email address, phone number, company name and anything you choose to include in a
      message, for example through our contact form or by email.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Account details:</strong> if you sign up for one of our apps, your name, email address or phone number, and your account settings.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Billing details:</strong> for paid plans, your billing details and payment records. Payments are handled by our payment partners or
      by the app store you buy through; we do not store full card details.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Information collected automatically</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Technical data:</strong> when you visit this website or use our products, we and our hosting providers may log your IP address,
      browser type, device information, pages visited and the date and time of your visit. We use this for security, troubleshooting and to keep
      our services reliable.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="how-we-use-it">3. How we use your information</h2>
  <p>We process personal data only for clear and lawful purposes, based on your consent or on legitimate uses permitted under the DPDP Act:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>to respond to your enquiries, business requests and partnership proposals;</li>
    <li>to create and manage your product accounts, and to provide, secure and support our products;</li>
    <li>to process payments and send invoices, service updates and important notices;</li>
    <li>to improve our products using aggregated or de-identified usage information;</li>
    <li>to prevent fraud, abuse and security incidents; and</li>
    <li>to comply with applicable laws, including tax and accounting obligations.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We send marketing emails only if you have agreed to receive them, and you can opt out at any time. <strong>We do not sell or rent your personal data.</strong>
  </p>

  <h2 id="product-data">4. Data you store in our apps</h2>
  <p>
    The content you add to our apps, such as tasks, notes, expenses or health entries, belongs to you. We process it only to provide, sync, secure
    and support the app for you, and we never sell it or use it for advertising. Health and financial information you choose to record is treated
    as sensitive: it is used only for the features you ask for. If you add information about other people, for example in a shared family list,
    please make sure they are comfortable with it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="sharing">5. Sharing and disclosure</h2>
  <p>We share personal data only when necessary, and only with:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Service providers</strong> who help us operate, such as cloud hosting, email delivery and payment processing, who are bound by
      confidentiality and data protection obligations;
    </li>
    <li><strong>Professional advisers</strong> such as auditors and legal counsel, where required; and</li>
    <li><strong>Government or law enforcement authorities</strong>, when we are required to do so by law.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Some service providers may process data outside India. Where they do, we take reasonable steps to keep your data protected and comply with
    any restrictions on cross-border transfers notified by the Government of India.
  </p>

  <h2 id="retention">6. Data retention</h2>
  <p>
    We keep personal data only for as long as it is needed for the purpose it was collected for. Account data is kept while your account is active
    and deleted after it is closed, except where we must keep records under applicable tax, accounting and LLP laws. Enquiries and messages
    are deleted once they are no longer needed.
  </p>

  <h2 id="security">7. How we protect your data</h2>
  <p>
    We use reasonable security safeguards, including encryption in transit and at rest, least-privilege access controls, regular backups and
    reputable infrastructure providers. No method of transmission or storage is completely secure, but we work hard to protect your data. If a
    personal data breach occurs, we will notify affected individuals and the Data Protection Board of India as required by law.
  </p>

  <h2 id="your-rights">8. Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under the DPDP Act, you have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Access</strong> a summary of the personal data we hold about you and how it is processed;</li>
    <li><strong>Correct, complete, update or erase</strong> your personal data;</li>
    <li><strong>Withdraw your consent</strong> at any time, as easily as you gave it (this does not affect processing already carried out);</li>
    <li><strong>Grievance redressal</strong> for any concern about how we handle your data; and</li>
    <li><strong>Nominate</strong> another person to exercise these rights on your behalf in the event of death or incapacity.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To exercise any of these rights, email <a href={`mailto:${officer.email}`}>{officer.email}</a>. We may need to verify your identity before
    acting on your request.
  </p>

  <h2 id="cookies">9. Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    We do not use advertising or cross-site tracking cookies. Our products use strictly necessary cookies to keep you signed in. See our{' '}
    <a href="/cookie-policy/">Cookie Policy</a> for details.
  </p>

  <h2 id="children">10. Children</h2>
  <p>
    Our apps are intended for people aged 18 and over. Under the DPDP Act, we need verifiable consent from a parent or lawful guardian before
    processing a child’s personal data. If you believe a child has shared personal data with us without that consent, please contact us and we
    will delete it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="grievance-officer">11. Grievance Officer</h2>
  <p>For any question, concern or complaint about this policy or how we handle your personal data, please contact our Grievance Officer:</p>
  <address class="panel my-6 p-5 text-sm leading-6 not-italic">
    <strong class="block text-base">{officer.name}</strong>
    <span class="block">{officer.designation}, {site.legalName}</span>
    <span class="block">Email: <a href={`mailto:${officer.email}`}>{officer.email}</a></span>
    {hasAddress && <span class="block">Address: {fullAddress}</span>}
  </address>
  <p>
    We will acknowledge your grievance promptly and respond within the period prescribed under applicable law. If you are not satisfied with our
    response, you may approach the Data Protection Board of India.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">12. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy from time to time. The “Last updated” date above shows when it was last revised. If we make significant changes,
    we will take reasonable steps to let you know.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
